(ns journey.pieces
  "The JOURNEY piece symbols.

   JOURNEY uses SOL's pieces, so these are SOL's own symbols, traced from the
   vector artwork in SOL_Player_Aids (the CHOOSE AN ACTION sheet), where each
   piece is drawn as white facets separated by thin dark contour lines.  Each
   symbol is reduced here to a single silhouette plus one polyline of contour
   lines, so it can be filled in any colour and scaled freely.

   Sizes are measured off that artwork and expressed as a fraction of the
   height of one board space, so `unit` is simply how tall a space is in
   whatever coordinates you are drawing in.  Draw every piece with the same
   unit and they come out in proportion to each other and to the board — the
   tower stands taller than a space, a sundiver a little over a third of one.

   Every symbol stands with its base on y = 0, rises into negative y, and is
   centred on x = 0.")

